ry in developing countries</article-title><source>Eye</source><year>2005</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>1083</fpage><lpage>1089</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.eye.6701966</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Yorston D (2005) High-volume surgery in developing countries. Eye 19:1083&#x02013;1089 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16304588</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR5"><label>5.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cox</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Presidential address: changing boundaries</article-title><source>J Thorac Cardiovasc Surg</source><year>2001</year><volume>122</volume><fpage>413</fpage><lpage>418</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1067/mtc.2001.118489</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Cox JL (2001) Presidential address: changing boundaries. J Thorac Cardiovasc Surg 122:413&#x02013;418 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11547286</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR6"><label>6.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rao</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pediatric cardiac surgery in developing countries</article-title><source>Pediatr Cardiol</source><year>2007</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>144</fpage><lpage>148</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00246-006-1452-7</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Rao SG (2007) Pediatric cardiac surgery in developing countries. Pediatr Cardiol 28:144&#x02013;148 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17486389</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mathers</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>Loncar</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Projections of global mortality a